==================================================================
--- doc/ttk_spinbox.n
+++ doc/ttk_spinbox.n
@@ -83,10 +83,39 @@
 .SH "VIRTUAL EVENTS"
 .PP
 The spinbox widget generates a \fB<<Increment>>\fR virtual event when
 the user presses <Up>, and a \fB<<Decrement>>\fR virtual event when the
 user presses <Down>.
+.SH "DEFAULT BINDINGS"
+.PP
+The spinbox widget has the same default bindings as the
+\fBttk::entry\fR widget, with the following differences:
+.IP \0\(bu 4
+Pressing mouse button 1 over the up or down arrow generates a
+\fB<<Increment>>\fR or \fB<<Decrement>>\fR virtual event
+respectively, and repeats it while the button is held down.
+.IP \0\(bu 4
+Double-clicking with mouse button 1 over the text area selects all of
+the text in the spinbox and positions the insert cursor at the end.
+Triple-clicking has no additional effect.
+.IP \0\(bu 4
+The Up and Down keys generate \fB<<Increment>>\fR and
+\fB<<Decrement>>\fR virtual events respectively.
+.IP \0\(bu 4
+Rotating the mouse wheel (or scrolling vertically on a touchpad)
+over the spinbox increments or decrements its value, even if the
+spinbox does not have the input focus.  Horizontal scrolling
+(\fB<Shift-MouseWheel>\fR) is ignored.
+To disable changing the value with the mouse wheel for a spinbox
+\fI.sb\fR, use for example:
+.CS
+bind .sb <MouseWheel> break
+bind .sb <Option-MouseWheel> break
+bind .sb <TouchpadScroll> break
+.CE
+.PP
+If the widget is disabled, none of the above actions occur.
 .SH "STYLING OPTIONS"
 .PP
 The class name for a \fBttk::spinbox\fP is \fBTSpinbox\fP.
 .PP
 Dynamic states: \fBactive\fP, \fBdisabled\fP, \fBfocus\fP, \fBreadonly\fP.

